  "confirmed_observations": [
    "Four substantial model-root component births occur at output Z 20.4, 21.8, 139.4 and 140.8 mm without overlapping lower support deposition.",
    "At these four roots the sampled first footprint/model intersection is about 0.95 or 1.05 mm below the extruded bead bottom; nominal 0.17 mm planes have zero footprint/model overlap.",
    "Two additional substantial support-interface islands appear at Z 24.6 and 25.8 mm, entirely left of the model minimum X and disconnected from the prior support footprint. Their exact generation stage requires further instrumentation.",
    "Two other tiny baseline candidates with area under 0.04 mm2 touch or nearly touch lower beads and are not counted as confirmed substantial islands.",
    "Setting XY clearance to zero in a disposable diagnostic project brings the model-root minimum centerline gaps to about 0.174 mm, while both external interface islands remain.",
    "Setting bottom Z clearance to zero leaves model-root gaps of about 0.84 mm. A Z-clearance-only adjustment does not resolve the defect.",
    "Disabling independent top-contact heights changes root shapes and lowers their sampled minimum gaps, but leaves both external interface islands. Independent top-contact height is not the sole cause."
  ],
  "reviewed_source_mechanisms": [
