      ],
      "finding": "The additional bottom-slice placeability filtering block is disabled with #if 0."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/libslic3r/Support/TreeSupport3D.cpp",
      "lines": [
        5044,
        5093
      ],
      "finding": "For nonzero bottom gaps, complete contact footprints are retained without requiring a placeable intersection; fallback contacts can be emitted even when clipped contacts are empty."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/libslic3r/Support/TreeModelVolumes.cpp",
      "lines": [
        641,
        651
      ],
      "finding": "Cached collision masks include XY clearance as well as neighboring layers for Z clearance. Clearance avoidance therefore cannot itself prove that a root is anchored."
    }
  ],
  "causal_limits": "Geometry and the single-parameter controls confirm a landing/clearance interaction. Source review identifies unsafe fallback mechanisms; no instrumented native source A/B isolates every contributing statement or the separate external-island generation stage.",
  "required_generic_correction": [
    "Choose a valid model landing or a build-plate-connected branch under the configured XY and Z constraints before accepting each root.",
    "Regenerate or reroute roots that cannot land, then validate extrusion-level component connectivity for both base and interface material.",
    "Retain the configured gaps and required overhang coverage; validate curved contacts, narrow interfaces, independent top heights and multiple printer profiles without device-name branches."
  ],
